{
 "note": "**The 1891 round, Lenton Road and Holles Crescent - schedules 170 to 177.** RG12/2682, transcribed by A. Hagues. **Read to close the 1891 holes**, which [[every-census-gap-and-where-to-start]] now puts ahead of everything else.\n\n**Five holes closed outright**, each a house the record held in 1881 and again in 1901 or 1911 but not in between:\n\n| schedule | house | who |\n|---|---|---|\n| 170 | **25 Lenton Road** | Hannah Maria Hopkins, her brother and two sisters - the household [[every-census-gap-and-where-to-start]] named as one of the six with the same family on both sides |\n| 171a | **29 Lenton Road** | Frederick Carver, lace manufacturer |\n| 172 | **31 Lenton Road** | Henry Clarke, lace manufacturer, at 48 in 1881 and 58 here |\n| 174 | **Cliff House** | George Parr, solicitor, with **eight children, two nieces and five servants** - seventeen in the house |\n| 175 | **Rock House, 37 Lenton Road** | Charles Shaw, 75, living on own means, who was 65 here in 1881 |\n\n**The numbers at the top of the page are hard to read** - 25, 27 and 29 could each be taken for 75, 77 and 79. They are settled by the households themselves: the Hopkins are at 25 in 1881 and 1901, Samuel Waite Johnson is at Lenton House, 27, in every other round, and the run is continuous.\n\n**Three households on these pages are deliberately left out**, because the record already holds them for 1891: Samuel Waite Johnson at **Lenton House (27 Lenton Road)**, James Bennett Gayton at **1 Holles Crescent**, and William Barrett at **1 Park Drive**.\n\n**One cannot be filed.** Schedule 180 gives **5 Park Drive** and the record has no number 5 - Park Drive runs 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 9. The household is Margaret King Allen, widow, whom the 1881 round puts at **3** Park Drive with the same daughter ten years younger. Left for now rather than moved on a guess.\n\n**Joseph Newbold the coachman** carries a street and no number, so he is unfiled. He was a coachman in The Park in 1871 too, in John Adams's household.",
 "source": "1891 census enumerator's book RG12/2682, Lenton Road and Holles Crescent, transcribed by A. Hagues.",
